rt of outlaw hangar gorgeous shot here  of the Mandalorian amongst the sunset  simultaneously conjuring images of a new  hope while showing the solitary life of  a bounty hunter it's also worth  mentioning here that the cinematography  is done by Greg Fraser who also did the  cinematography for row 1 and this next  image here screams the first 10 minutes  of that film now we don't know who these  two are but they are obviously hiding  from someone and this woman is trying to  protect the child if I were to take a  random guess this is a flashback of the  Mandalorian as a child with his mother  with an entire season to fill the show  will undoubtedly go into how the  Mandalorian became a bounty hunter a man  with no family eking out a dangerous  life on the edge of the galaxy this next  shot here looks as though they're  shooting at the woman and child but it's  an editing fake out the background  really doesn't match  this is likely an altercation in one of  the trade towns and these troopers here  are under the control of Giancarlo  Esposito zkk Erik tur we don't have a  name for his character yet but in an  interview with slash film he said the  following in a way you might call him an  underworld character you may also look  at him as a savior as someone who might  bring back some order to the world after  it's all collapsed so it's not known  whether he's some sort of Imperial  commander trying to keep his soldiers  together or the leader of a world which  is now impoverished after the defeat of  the Empire and here is our first full-on  face shot of the Mandalorian a  particular note here is the butt end of  his rifle which was shared on Instagram  by Jon Favreau in October of last year  November 12th the release date on Disney  Plus Disney's new online platform  similar to Netflix and that date can't  come fast enough here we have two  characters and what appears to be a  flare looking for rescue and someone  coming to help riding an imperial  speeder with the